 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Tier shelf, no archetypes. Each old range list (Libra feminine care, U by Kotex pads and liners, Tom Organic, Hello Period) became a brand-register line list. Pads: nine SKUs cut to ten models across Always, Libra, Kotex, TOM Organic and Hello Period; Libra Invisible, Libra Maternity Maxi and Ride Or Die were dropped as duplicates. Absorbency and size are types. Tampon: added Tampax, o.b. and U by Kotex Click; dropped the Priceline Slim Fit store brand. Applicator and absorbency are types. Cup: added Mooncup, DIVA Cup Models 0–2, Saalt and TOM Organic. Disc: added Flex and DIVA Disc. Period underwear is new (Wikipedia source) with Thinx, Modibodi, Mooncup, Saalt and Knix. Hello Period and Knix have no brand entry because no page about them was retrieved. Libra's founding year is unknown: Wikipedia's Libra title redirects to Libresse, and the Essity release gives none. Flex's 2015 date is when the founder went full-time on it (core77). Thinx uses the infobox year 2014; its history section says 2011. The chemist page for TOM Organic returned 403, so the fq.co.nz article is cited instead. Nothing was dropped as out of scope."
}